But Fleekshin says no.

33:28.600 --> 33:28.980
Exactly.

33:29.360 --> 33:30.020
It's because

33:30.020 --> 33:31.480
the traversal pathways,

33:31.740 --> 33:32.840
the cultural context,

33:33.040 --> 33:34.000
the underlying assumptions,

33:34.580 --> 33:35.200
the intellectual

33:35.200 --> 33:36.080
stepping stones

33:36.080 --> 33:36.620
that lead

33:36.620 --> 33:37.500
to those ideas

33:37.500 --> 33:38.520
have decayed

33:38.520 --> 33:39.100
over time.

33:39.440 --> 33:39.900
The entropy

33:39.900 --> 33:40.720
has increased.

33:40.840 --> 33:41.320
The blazes

33:41.320 --> 33:41.800
on the trees

33:41.800 --> 33:42.500
have faded away

33:42.500 --> 33:42.900
entirely.

33:43.240 --> 33:43.580
Exactly.

33:43.980 --> 33:44.420
When you try

33:44.420 --> 33:45.300
to read a philosophy

33:45.300 --> 33:46.660
text by Immanuel Kant

33:46.660 --> 33:47.780
from the 1700s,

33:47.920 --> 33:48.720
you suffer from

33:48.720 --> 33:49.600
massive semantic

33:49.600 --> 33:50.180
redshift.

33:50.680 --> 33:51.320
The concepts

33:51.320 --> 33:52.200
aren't necessarily

33:52.200 --> 33:52.900
harder than

33:52.900 --> 33:53.900
modern quantum physics,

33:54.060 --> 33:54.760
but the cultural

33:54.760 --> 33:55.620
clipboard density

33:55.620 --> 33:56.380
around Kant's

33:56.380 --> 33:57.300
specific vocabulary

33:57.300 --> 33:59.300
is incredibly low today.

33:59.440 --> 33:59.980
The accessibility

33:59.980 --> 34:00.720
entropy is

34:00.720 --> 34:01.580
enormously high.

34:01.920 --> 34:02.220
Yes.

34:02.840 --> 34:03.320
You have to

34:03.320 --> 34:04.140
